    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f76120df_4ab4b50d",
        "filename": "apex/prebuilt.go",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-27T13:59:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Aren\u0027t the dex2oat commands with all their inputs and outputs known in Soong?\n\nNo. Unfortunately, some of them are generated by Make using dexpreopt_gen.\n\nBesides, even if all dex2oat commands are generated by Soong, Soong still won\u0027t know whether the artifacts will eventually exist in the system image or not. Soong outputs the artifacts to an intermediate folder, and does not know if they are actually installed (i.e., packed into the system image) or not. The installation is handled by make. These lines are for passing this information to make so that make can handle it. It could be possible that make goes wrong and does not install the artifacts. Soong will never know.",
      "parentUuid": "e45ce1b1_f9b1a433",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 188,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "204356f3b54be5936e152815a96d1e917022d077",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40cdee15_7a769909",
        "filename": "apex/prebuilt.go",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-27T14:26:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, this was only about it being a build failure, not necessarily a Soong failure. What I\u0027d expect to happen if I were to delete this if statement is that some make targets would be missing so ninja would complain about missing dependencies. I didn\u0027t expect it to just silently continue without dexpreopting, that\u0027s not how ninja usually operates.\n\nIf it\u0027s dexpreopt_gen or its output script that puts the last dependencies in place then isn\u0027t it a matter of error checks there? Maybe we can add a flag to make them more strict?",
      "parentUuid": "f76120df_4ab4b50d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 188,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "204356f3b54be5936e152815a96d1e917022d077",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7dc4a5de_06d3436c",
        "filename": "apex/prebuilt.go",
